              "addressed_to": "",
              "display_name": "Assistant",
              "text": "Your **Notes settings** control how CHA processes note text and generates note audio:\n\n- **Compression provider** \u2014 the model provider used to compress notes, format imported web pages and YouTube content, and create saved conversation summaries. These operations fail if no usable provider is selected.\n- **Reasoning effort** \u2014 how much reasoning the compression provider is asked to use. The default is **High**. This setting has no effect with native Google (Gemini) or Anthropic providers.\n- **Audio service URL** \u2014 the service CHA contacts to generate audio for notes.\n- **Audio API key** \u2014 the saved key used to authenticate with that audio service. Note audio requires both the URL and key and runs only in the desktop application.\n\nWeb-page imports also depend on the page-reading service configured under **Search API**.\n\nThese settings are separate from character providers and chat speech voices. You can check background compression and audio results in **Events**.\n\nI haven\u2019t inspected your saved settings; I can also show you which providers and services your Notes currently use.",
